[com33]
type=text
x=311
y=43
width=119
height=245
parent_id=com33
text_font=quill_oblique_large
text=A History of the Goblin Race
text_halign=1
color=3421218

[com34]
type=layer
width=512
height=388

[com35]
type=text
x=56
y=40
width=187
height=116
parent_id=com38
text_font=q8_full
text=Goblin tradition holds that<br>their race was created by<br>a war-god in order to<br>fight a war against other<br>gods.
text_valign=1

[com36]
type=text
x=54
y=159
width=191
height=131
parent_id=com38
text_font=q8_full
text=(They never name their<br>god, so whether it is the<br>same as any of the gods<br>worshipped by the other<br>races is unknown.)
text_valign=1

[com37]
type=text
x=275
y=39
width=183
height=128
parent_id=com38
text_font=q8_full
text=The legends also speak<br>of goblins fighting<br>against goblins during<br>the wars, so it is likely<br>that gods other than<br>their creators used<br>them as footsoldiers.
text_valign=1

[com38]
type=text
x=275
y=166
width=191
height=123
parent_id=com38
text_font=q8_full
text=Although goblins are still<br>warlike, it is probable<br>that in earlier ages<br>they were more<br>organised than they<br>are now,
text_valign=1

[com39]
type=layer
width=512
height=388
flags=1

[com40]
type=text
x=61
y=35
width=174
height=96
parent_id=com42
text_font=q8_full
text=especially if they were<br>under the direct<br>command of one or<br>more gods.
text_halign=1
text_valign=1

[com41]
type=text
x=47
y=144
width=199
height=133
parent_id=com42
text_font=q8_full
text=This is corroborated<br>by finds unearthed<br>at various<br>archaeological sites,<br>including the large<br>excavation east of<br>Varrock.
text_halign=1
text_valign=1

[com42]
type=text
x=278
y=39
width=176
height=132
parent_id=com42
text_font=q8_full
text=Armour and weapons<br>have been found,<br>obviously made to fit<br>goblins but far more<br>well-made than their<br>current equipment.
text_halign=1
text_valign=1

[com43]
type=layer
width=512
height=388
flags=1

[com44]
type=text
x=60
y=43
width=184
height=235
parent_id=com46
text_font=q8_full
text=Almost every piece of<br>ancient goblin equipment<br>has one of a number<br>of symbols on it,<br>and by correlating these<br>symbols with the<br>sketchy records that<br>survive from the<br>Third Age it has been<br>possible to identify<br>twelve distinct goblin tribes<br>or regiments.

[com45]
type=text
x=277
y=44
width=182
height=148
parent_id=com46
text_font=q8_full
text=The separate identities of<br>the tribes have long<br>since dissolved and<br>no goblins remember the<br>symbols, although their<br>generals may still<br>recognize the ancient<br>tribal names.

[com46]
type=text
x=277
y=192
width=192
height=89
parent_id=com46
text_font=q8_full
text=In the following pages<br>I present a list of<br>the tribes and their<br>symbols.

